    "answer": "Key Insight 1: Residents dump trash in waterways mainly because garbage trucks cannot access narrow alleys, leading to health risks inside homes.\n\nKey Insight 2: Households are willing to segregate waste if the barangay provides clear schedules and color-coded bins, ensuring trash is collected promptly.\n\nKey Insight 3: Community members value cleanliness but need reliable systems to avoid leaving waste exposed on the street.\n\nInfluence on the Plan\nThese insights highlight that the plan must prioritize accessible collection systems (e.g., smaller vehicles for alleys, fixed schedules) and segregation support (color-coded bins). By combining infrastructure adjustments with clear communication, the barangay can reduce creek dumping, improve sanitation, and encourage residents to actively participate in waste management.",
